### E.5 Row Level Security policies
Enable RLS on every table above (`alter table X enable row level security;`), then:

```sql
-- Helper: is the current user an admin?
create function public.is_admin() returns boolean as $$
  select exists (select 1 from public.profiles where id = auth.uid() and role = 'admin');
$$ language sql stable security definer;

-- Profiles: citizens see only themselves; admins see all
create policy "own profile" on public.profiles for select using (id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());
create policy "update own profile" on public.profiles for update using (id = auth.uid());

-- Schemes / eligibility_rules / document_requirements: publicly readable (not sensitive), admin-writable
create policy "schemes readable" on public.schemes for select using (true);
create policy "schemes admin write" on public.schemes for all using (public.is_admin());
-- (repeat the readable/admin-write pair for eligibility_rules and document_requirements)

-- Citizen-owned tables: isolate by citizen_id, admin bypass
create policy "own documents" on public.documents for all using (citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());
create policy "own applications" on public.applications for all using (citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());
create policy "own agent_runs" on public.agent_runs for all using (citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());
create policy "own notifications" on public.notifications for all using (citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());
create policy "own consent" on public.consent_records for all using (citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin());

-- agent_events / audit_logs: readable if you own the parent run, or you're admin
create policy "agent_events via run" on public.agent_events for select
  using (exists (select 1 from public.agent_runs r where r.id = run_id and (r.citizen_id = auth.uid() or public.is_admin())));
create policy "audit_logs via run" on public.audit_logs for select
  using (public.is_admin() or exists (select 1 from public.agent_runs r where r.id = run_id and r.citizen_id = auth.uid()));
```

Test this explicitly (see E.9) — RLS mistakes are the #1 way hackathon demos break live ("why can't Rahul see his own application?").

### E.6 Storage
- Create a `documents` bucket, **not public**.
- Storage policy: a citizen can upload/read/delete only under a path prefixed with their own `auth.uid()`, e.g. `documents/{citizen_id}/{filename}`. Enforce this via a Storage RLS policy matching `storage.foldername(name)[1] = auth.uid()::text`.
- Store the resulting path in `documents.file_path`; generate signed URLs on read rather than making the bucket public.

